.TH ESWORD4LINUX 1 "November 2026" "esword4linux 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
esword4linux \- native reader for e-Sword modules on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esword4linux
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esword4linux
opens e-Sword modules (Bible, commentary, dictionary, lexicon, topic,
devotional, harmony, map and reference databases) from one user-selected
folder. The files are opened read-only and are never modified.
.PP
No modules are bundled. On first run the application asks for the modules
folder; cancelling exits without opening a window.
.PP
The application uses a private Python and Qt runtime under
.I /opt/esword4linux
and the distribution's
.I /usr/bin/python3
interpreter. It does not install packages into the system Python environment.
.SH OPTIONS
The application has no command-line options. Qt platform selection can be
overridden with the standard
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
environment variable (for example
.I xcb
or
.I wayland
).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/esword4linux/settings.json
User preferences and the selected modules folder.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/esword4linux/catalog.db
Module metadata and indexing state.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/esword4linux/content.db
Optional full-text search index.
.PP
The XDG_CONFIG_HOME and XDG_CACHE_HOME environment variables are honored.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Optional Qt platform override. Unset by default so Qt selects X11 or Wayland
from the current session.
.TP
.B ESWORD4LINUX_ROOT
Optional runtime-root override, used for testing and portable builds. The
installed package uses
.IR /opt/esword4linux .
.SH SEE ALSO
The installed documentation is in
.I /usr/share/doc/esword4linux/
and the upstream project is at
.IR https://github.com/felotrrs/esword4linux .
